    "source": {
      "revision": 1,
      "rules": "2024",
      "custom": "Bad Eden"
    },
    "tags": [],
    "description": {
      "value": "<p><em>\"The future is just memory pointed the other way.\"</em></p>\n<p>The Dreamwalker reads the Tree and works manifestations \u2014 and that work <em>is</em> the fuel. You run on <strong>Surge</strong> like everyone, but yours arrives when you <strong>cast a manifestation</strong> (bank +1, max +2/round). The old sprawl folds into this: the old Echo Dice fold into Surge, the eight soma-break feats live on as four tier powers \u2014 and the <strong>Dream Echo Reservoir</strong> endures as its own vessel: store a manifestation, release it later at no base cost.</p>\n<h3>The Oracle (spent via Surge)</h3>\n<ul>\n  <li><strong>Omen</strong> (1) \u2014 you or an ally saw the thread coming: banks a reroll-lowest.</li>\n  <li><strong>Dream Ward</strong> (2) \u2014 an ally drifts into a protective dreamstate: DR + a reroll.</li>\n  <li><strong>Shared Dream</strong> (3) \u2014 allies within 6 squares bank a reroll and draw 1 Clarity (refuels their casting).</li>\n  <li><strong>Reality Hack</strong> (5) \u2014 rewrite the moment: the party banks a reroll and one enemy rolls its next attack at disadvantage.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>The <strong>Dream-Cache</strong> endures \u2014 bank a manifestation between scenes, deploy it next scene without paying Clarity. And the oracle's quiet work stays out of combat: Dream Resonance still senses a hex's Sephirah, and you still Commune with the Great Work for a true answer.</p>",
      "chat": ""
    },
